[38;5;247mFixed horizontal overflow on phones (360px/412px viewports) caused by flex children expanding beyond viewport width.[0m
[38;5;247m### Changes[0m
[38;5;247m- Added `html, body { overflow-x: clip }` as a safety net in `web/src/styles.css`.[0m
[38;5;247m- Added `min-width: 0` to all flex container chains: `.app`, `.top`, `.brand`, `.brand > div`, `.brand p`, `.matchup`, `.win-bar`, `.win-bar-main`, `.demo-banner`, `.demo-controls` — preventing flex items from inheriting the too-wide min-content size.[0m
[38;5;247m- At ≤600px: added `max-width: 100%` to `.top > *`, `flex-wrap: wrap` to `.brand`, `white-space: nowrap` + `text-overflow: ellipsis` on `.brand h1` and `.brand p`, `max-width: 100%` on `.matchup select`, `flex-wrap: wrap` on `.matchup .roster-toggle`.[0m
[38;5;247m- At ≤412px: hid `.brand p` (`display: none`) so the long subtitle no longer forces width.[0m
[38;5;247m- Added `overflow: hidden` + `text-overflow: ellipsis` on `.win-bar-team` and `flex-shrink: 0` on `.demo-step-count`.[0m
[38;5;247m### Root cause[0m
[38;5;247mThe header (`.top`) is a flex container. Its children (`.brand`, `.matchup`) had no `min-width: 0`, so their min-content size (driven by unwrappable text like the subtitle paragraph and button labels) forced the entire header wider than the viewport. Every full-width descendant inherited this oversized box.[0m
